  <Properties>
    <blocks>
      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "contentData": [
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "30a0d072-7837-449e-9db2-228afed80595",
      "key": "1c9a4f30-2b7e-4d61-8a03-9f2c5e7a1b44",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "heading",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": ""
        },
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EThe University of California and California State University campuses no longer require SAT or ACT scores for admission.\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EIf you plan to apply to a private university, check that school\u0027s admission requirements. Some private colleges still require or recommend a test score.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch3\u003ERegistering for the SAT\u003C/h3\u003E\u003Col\u003E\u003Cli\u003EGo to \u003Ca href=\u0022https://satsuite.collegeboard.org/sat/registration\u0022 target=\u0022_blank\u0022 rel=\u0022noopener\u0022\u003Esatsuite.collegeboard.org\u003C/a\u003E and create a College Board account, or sign in to an existing one.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EChoose \u0026quot;Register\u0026quot; and pick your test date and centre.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EFollow the directions and read each question carefully.\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ol\u003E\u003Ch4\u003EWhile you register\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAnswer the questions about your academic and personal interests. College Board uses them to connect you with colleges and scholarship opportunities.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EWait to enter a fee-waiver code until the form asks for it. See your counsellor to find out if you qualify for one.\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003Ch3\u003ESending your scores\u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003EColleges do not receive your scores automatically. You choose the recipients.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EEvery registration includes four free score sends.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EOrder your free sends no later than nine days after the test date.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAfter nine days, each score report costs $12.00 per school.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EEvery college sets its own score deadline. Check each admission website so your scores arrive in time.\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003Ch4\u003ECal State and UC applicants\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003ECal State campuses are test-free. You do not send SAT or ACT scores with a Cal State Apply application.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EUC campuses are also test-free for admission. If you send scores to one UC campus, every UC campus can see them.\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003Ch3\u003EWhen should you take the SAT?\u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003ETake it in May or June of your junior year.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ELeave room for one or two retakes in the autumn of your senior year.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EFor most colleges, the December test date of senior year is the practical cut-off.\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003Cp\u003ENot sure where to apply yet? Use \u003Ca href=\u0022https://bigfuture.collegeboard.org\u0022 target=\u0022_blank\u0022 rel=\u0022noopener\u0022\u003EBigFuture\u003C/a\u003E to explore colleges and build a list.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
